  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday morning through next Friday) Issued at 228 PM EDT Sat \nOct 3 2026\n\nThe front lingers across far southern Georgia Tuesday and Wednesday. \nThere is some uncertainty as to how much rain the very southern \ncounties of our CWA will get as we move into next week. Forecast \ntotals range from a half an inch to an additional two inches until \nthe front is pushed off to the east on Wednesday. \n\nFor a majority of the area however, rain is expected to come to an \nend overnight Tuesday morning. Dry air will settle in across much of \nthe area north of a line from Columbus to Augusta with high \ntemperatures in the mid to upper 70s. Overnight lows will fall into \nthe 50s with 40's likely in the higher elevations of northern \nGeorgia. By the time we get to Thursday, rain chances for the CWA \ndrop to nearly zero. \n\nLong term models indicate that we'll be going into a weekly pattern \nas another short wave gets set to move through the upper level flow \nby next weekend which should bring showers and maybe a thunderstorm \nback into the forecast. &&",
